st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.


Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

Credits
-------
Based on Aurélien APTEL <aurelien dot aptel at gmail dot com> bt source code.

My changes
----------
If by some bizarre chance you happened upon this repo, I added these patches:
newterm
delkey 
centered anysize 
newterm tmux
scrollback 
mousescrollback
scrollback mouse altscreen (scrollback for specific programs)
scroll reflow - very important. keeps text from being eliminated
                if the window is resized (e.g., moved from master to stack)
blinking cursor
themed cursor
xresources
colorschemes

Hacks:
- xresources
  * colorscheme: the theme number of startup colorscheme
  * lightmode, darkmode: theme number of colorscheme for dark / light mode
  * daystart, nightstart: hours for st to start in the dark or light mode
  * autotimetheme: boolean (0 or 1) to enable auto dark/light mode
  = In theory the signal handler could trigger a time check
  = I stopped caring about auto dark/light mode.  I work in many different
    locations now, so ambient light conditions matter more than time of day.

- colorschemes
  * Added signal handling (SIGUSR1) to change theme at runtime
  * Added optional fg/bg colors (color array indices 258 and 259)

schemesel themes:
0: st default, 1: candle dark, 2: rose pine, 3: rose pine dawn
4: solarized dark, 5: solarized light, 6: tomorrow night blue, 7: acme,
8: moonfly, 9: gruvbox dark, 10: gruvbox light,
11: selenized black, 12: selenized white,
13: selenized dark, 14: selenized light, 15: equilibrium

